# Supercombo Wiki — Avatar Legends Offline Mirror

A small Python script that mirrors the **Avatar Legends** section of [wiki.supercombo.gg](https://wiki.supercombo.gg/w/Avatar_Legends) for offline reading. Runs on a schedule (e.g. daily) and only re-downloads pages that have changed. Pages whose title contains "Zaheer" are seeded first, so a fresh or interrupted run captures that character before anything else.

The output is plain HTML with all images/CSS/JS, viewable in any browser — no server needed. Just open `~/supercombo_mirror/index.html`.

This mirror follows the exact same design as the Dustloop GGST mirror in this repo (see `readme` / `dustloop_mirror.py`); see that document for the full rationale. This file only covers what's different for Supercombo.

---

## Requirements

- **Python 3.8+**
- **wget**

Verify it works: `wget --version`

---

## First run

```bash
python supercombo_mirror.py
```

When it's done you'll have:

```
~/supercombo_mirror/
├── index.html        ← open this (redirects to Avatar Legends, links straight to Zaheer if present)
├── mirror.log         ← run history
└── site/
    ├── w/             ← wiki pages
    ├── images/        ← character art, hitboxes, etc.
    └── ...
```

Subsequent runs are much faster because wget's `--timestamping` flag skips files that haven't changed on the server.

