## How the page-discovery + Zaheer priority works

Same mechanism as the Dustloop mirror: `wget`'s recursive crawl only finds pages reachable by following links from pages it's already downloaded, so an orphaned subpage could be missed forever. Every run instead asks the wiki's own API (`action=query&list=allpages` with `apprefix=Avatar_Legends`) for the complete, current list of Avatar Legends page titles, and feeds that list to `wget` as explicit seed URLs in addition to the normal recursive crawl.

That seed list is sorted so any title containing "zaheer" (case-insensitive) comes first. `--timestamping` means pages already on disk and unchanged are a cheap conditional check, so re-running never wastes time re-fetching Zaheer once it's captured — but on the very first run, or after cache eviction, Zaheer's pages are the first thing downloaded, not the last.

If the wiki's API is unreachable when a run starts, the script logs a warning and falls back to the plain recursive crawl from `BASE_URL` — it never fails the whole run over this, it just loses the priority ordering and orphan-page guarantee for that run.

