## Serving it locally

`supercombo_mirror/server.py` works the same way as the Dustloop one — it translates wiki-style URLs (including query strings and thumbnail fallbacks) to the files wget actually saved, and patches in a CSS fix for MediaWiki's Tabber extension so movelist tabs don't collapse to a single hidden panel:

```bash
cd ~/supercombo_mirror
python /path/to/repo/supercombo_mirror/server.py 8001
```

Then open `http://localhost:8001/`.

---

## Customization

All settings are at the top of `supercombo_mirror.py`:

| Setting | Default | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `BASE_URL` | `.../w/Avatar_Legends` | Change to mirror a different Supercombo game section |
| `PRIORITY_SUBSTRING` | `"zaheer"` | Case-insensitive title substring downloaded first |
| `OUTPUT_DIR` | `~/supercombo_mirror` | Where files go |
| `WAIT_BETWEEN_REQUESTS` | `1` | Seconds between requests. **Don't lower this.** |
| `INCLUDE_DIRS` | wiki + assets | Paths wget is allowed to descend into |
| `REJECT_REGEX` | edit/history/etc. | URL patterns to skip (saves a lot of space) |

